,{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00284","title":["ProGIC: Progressive and Lightweight Generative Image Compression with Residual Vector Quantization"],"author":[{"given":"Hao","family":"Cao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Tsinghua University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chengbin","family":"Liang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tsinghua University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wenqi","family":"Guo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tsinghua University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhijin","family":"Qin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tsinghua University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jungong","family":"Han","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tsinghua University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00284","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:18:49Z","timestamp":1791487129000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698221.pdf?arnumber=11698221","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00738","title":["Continual Adaptation of Vision Foundational Models for Semantic Segmentation in Adverse Weather"],"author":[{"given":"Nikhil Kumar","family":"Jangamreddy","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mahsa","family":"Baktashmotlagh","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Queensland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chetan","family":"Arora","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Delhi"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00738","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:33:07Z","timestamp":1791487987000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698440.pdf?arnumber=11698440","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.29141\/2949-477x-2026-5-3-1","title":["Comparative analysis of image augmentation methods for improving the quality of computer vision models in animal husbandry"],"author":[{"given":"Irina I.","family":"Mikhailenko","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Belgorod Federal Scientific Center of the Russian Academy of Sciences, Belgorod, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>The research is aimed at developing robust computer vision models for precision animal husbandry tasks (health monitoring, animal identification, and body condition scoring), which are commonly hampered by a scarcity of labeled data. Collecting and annotating images in real-life farm conditions is an expensive and labor-intensive process. Data augmentation methods are a key solution for expanding training sets and improving the generalization capability of models. This paper examines several methods for preprocessing cattle image data and explores augmentation methods that use the pre-existing data to generate new data and enrich training data without human intervention, thereby enhancing performance. The experiments have addressed various aspects of data scarcity, yielding competitive results that provide a baseline for future research.<\/jats:p>","URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.29141\/2949-477x-2026-5-3-1","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T03:57:00Z","timestamp":1791431820000}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00194","title":["PURESPACE: A Benchmark for Abstract Spatial Reasoning in Vision-Language Models"],"author":[{"given":"Jinkai","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhenliang","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Lifeng","family":"Fan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wei","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00194","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:28:03Z","timestamp":1791487683000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698349.pdf?arnumber=11698349","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.11709274","title":["FDM-Net: A High-Frequency-Aware Depth-Guided Multi-Scale Fusion Network for Lightweight Image Super-Resolution"],"author":[{"given":"Yanying","family":"Liu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei University of Technology","place":["Wuhan, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Fang","family":"Wan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei University of Technology","place":["Wuhan, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhiwei","family":"Ye","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei University of Technology","place":["Wuhan, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.1170927