n-Language Models for Automated 3D PET\/CT Report Generation"],"author":[{"given":"Wenpei","family":"Jiao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Medical Technology and National Biomedical Imaging Center, Peking University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ke","family":"Yan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"DAMO Academy, Alibaba Group"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jiajin","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"DAMO Academy, Alibaba Group"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dakai","family":"Jin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"DAMO Academy, Alibaba Group"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhaoheng","family":"Xie","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Medical Technology and National Biomedical Imaging Center, Peking University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00509","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:20:59Z","timestamp":1791487259000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698223.pdf?arnumber=11698223","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00731","title":["Task-Specific Knowledge Improves Generalization: A Logits-Based Framework for Continual Learning of Vision-Language Models"],"author":[{"given":"Sijie","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Computer Science and Software Engineering, Shenzhen University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yingying","family":"Zhu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Computer Science and Software Engineering, Shenzhen University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00731","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:27:56Z","timestamp":1791487676000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11697668.pdf?arnumber=11697668","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.20944\/preprints202610.0848.v1","title":["Calibrated Yes\/No Visual Decisions with Small Open Vision-Language Models: A Pre-Registered Benchmark of 12 Models, Plug-In Heads, and an Airline Baggage Case Study"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-8268-8667","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hasan","family":"Tatar","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>Many industrial vision questions are binary (\"is this suitcase damaged?\") and must be answered on premises, with a confidence that can be trusted and an option to defer to a human. We study how far small open vision-language models (VLMs) get on such questions and what it takes to make them reliable. First, a pre-registered benchmark of 12 open VLMs (0.8B-12B parameters; 1,807 yes\/no items in four question families; test split analysed once) on an NVIDIA Jetson AGX Orin finds flat discrimination among the Qwen-based models of 2B parameters and above (pooled test AUROC 0.930-0.940), no gain from models post-trained for decisions over their own base models, and calibration that varies far more across models than ranking does: raw expected calibration error ranges from 0.014 to 0.122, and one shared Platt step brings every model to 0.013-0.037. Qwen3-VL-2B is the fastest model (0.45 s per image, 4.4 GB), and no model was significantly better than it in any tested comparison. Second, we attach per-task heads, L2-regularised logistic regressions on the frozen model's last-layer hidden state, and abstain below a confidence threshold set by the application. On test photos from sources unseen in training, a suitcase-damage head raises AUROC from 0.925 (calibrated model answer) to 0.962, paired 95% CI of the gain [+0.018, +0.058]; at a 0.90 threshold it answers 71.7% of the photos with 96.6% accuracy, against 61.1% for the calibrated answer. A baggage-presence head does not improve AUROC. Third, a case study runs the calibrated model on an 8 GB laptop: on 148 test photos it decides 49% automatically at 97.3% accuracy and leaves the rest to staff, at no API cost. Limitations: internet photos only, four question families, and a source confound in one damage test set.<\/jats:p>","URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.20944\/preprints202610.0848.v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,10]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,12]],"date-time":"2026-10-12T05:37:37Z","timestamp":1791783457000}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icsseecc69062.2026.11722231","title":["A Lightweight Vision-Based Framework for Yoga Pose Detection and Corrective Feedback"],"author":[{"given":"Vaishnavi","family":"S","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"PSG Institute of Technology and Applied Research","place":["Coimbatore, India"],"department":["Department of Computer Science and Engineering"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kamal Chander","family":"R","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"PSG Institute of Technology and Applied Research","place":["Coimbatore, India"],"department":["Department of Computer Science and Engineering"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kamal","family":"S","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"PSG Institute of Technology and Applied Research","place":["Coimbatore, India"],"department":["Department of Computer Science and Engineering"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Aniruddh","family":"Muralidaran","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"PSG Institute of Technology and Applied Research","place":["Coimbatore, India"],"department":["Department of Computer Science and Engineering"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icsseecc69062.2026.11722231","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,12]],"date-time":"2026-10-12T19:12:57Z","timestamp":1791832377000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11721520\/11721985\/11722231.pdf?arnumber=11722231","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00227","title":["Reliable Test-Time Adaptation via Evidential Uncertainty Modeling in Vision-Language Models"],"author":[{"given":"Yiwei","family":"You","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, University of International Business and Economics"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zan","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, University of International Business and Economics"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Bo","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, University of International Business and Economics"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Xiaofei","family":"Zhou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Information Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00227","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:19:50Z","timestamp":1791487190000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11697784.pdf?arnumber=11697784","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","in